{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1079903-immortal-eyes-questions-opinions-ramifications","id":1079903,"title":"Immortal Eyes Questions: Opinions & Ramifications","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-17T11:39:36-07:00","id":1079903,"title":"Immortal Eyes Questions: Opinions & Ramifications","content":"Just posing a few questions:<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever actually played through THE IMMORTAL EYES Trilogy? Even more so, has anyone actually run it? I want to run it for my group, but am interested in whether anyone actually enjoyed playing / running it.<br /> <br /> Also, do we think that we are going to get another adventure resource book based on the new novel that is being written for C20?<br /> <br /> Will there be a way to convert the old trilogy plot line to make it playable with the revised system? I guess I'm used to tinkering with the system &amp; cobbling out house rules when it comes to Changeling, anyway. I was just hoping that there will be an official word or conversion section on how to translate the old books.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> Opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12375-wratticusq","name":"Wratticusq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:02:45-07:00","id":1079916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wratticusq</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1079903-immortal-eyes-questions-opinions-ramifications#post1079903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do we think that we are going to get another adventure resource book based on the new novel that is being written for C20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never say never, but I wouldn't count on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was just hoping that there will be an official word or conversion section on how to translate the old books. </div> </div> </div>This is by no means an official word on the subject, but I just don't see the changes from second edition to the 20th anniversary edition being big enough to warrant anything like that. I mean, it's still the same Storyteller base system used in all the World of Darkness game lines throughout all of their editions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T21:18:38-07:00","id":1080179,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: I may be wrong about everything.<br /> <br /> Immortal Eyes as a campaign seems to be barely coherent without reading the fictional trilogy.<br /> <br /> The general setting parts are ok and even may be useful, but plotwise it's supposed to allow player characters to work behind the scenes of the main story, which is a bit strange approach. There is an optional to take on roles of main characters of the story, but game warns, that they are completely broken, compared to normal newly generated characters.<br /> <br /> I would advise reading Immortal Eyes trilogy (for Storyteller), it's pretty decent. Then, you can use a campaign setting parts complete with local NPCs for retelling this story anew or making the one of your own. Or taking suggested campaign route.<br /> <br /> As a foundation and source of inspiration, Immortal Eyes are great. We started our own campaign a few years back, using Toys will be Toys scenario as an inciting incident.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 04-20-2017, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T04:57:30-07:00","id":1081388,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure it's totally relevant for the thread, but I thought this might be interest you: here is a post I've written for the Changeling group on Facebook.<br /> <br /> I wanted to share something with you all. It is a memory.<br /> <br /> Back in 1995, just prior to the release of Changeling: the Dreaming, an advertisement leaflet was distributed. There had been already several announcements in different WW sourcebooks about Changeling. But this leaflet was in itself a promise to transport us to different places, to a magical world. I remember reading it over and over, peeking at the gorgeous illustrations (the map of Concordia! Oh I loved that map!) and imagining how terrific this game was going to be.<br /> <br /> When it finally came out, in the middle of summer, I went to my RPG store dressed as an elf to buy it (true story), and then my brother and I went on a surf trip for two weeks. I remember that I was reading at the same time (and for the first time) the Lord of the Rings.<br /> <br /> And back in September for my first year at the university, I launched my first Changeling games. It was magical.<br /> <br /> But you know what? One of the things I best remember from this time was the Toybox, the novel written by Jackie Cassada. This novel accompanied me during all my commuting in bus, during every little moment between classes. I read it over and over and over again. Since then, the characters have stayed with me -- Morgan, Leigh, Valmont, Rasputin, Tor, Edmund and also Glynis and Duke Aeon and, of course, Yrtalien.<br /> <br /> I have to say that my favourite characters were Morgan, Tor and Yrtalien. I loved Morgan and Tor's relationship, I loved, really loved, Tor as a Vietnam vet haunted by his past which was synonymous with Banality. In a wonderful twist of the usual Forgetting conundrum for changelings, Tor's Forgetting of his fae self meant that he remembered his human past as a solider in an ugly and traumatic war. I thought that it fitted so well what a troll was in the game, that it forever shaped my imagination of what a Seelie troll should be.<br /> <br /> Morgan's past was also very mysterious and made me very curious: apparently she was a reincarnation of the sister of Queen Nuala of Munster (as we learned later in Court of all Kings), killed during the Battle of Pacifica.<br /> <br /> And, finally, there was Yrtalien. Gallant, dashing, dark, powerful, cruel, and learning fast, Yrtalien was all an Unseelie prince of the Shadow Court could be -- and more.<br /> <br /> And you what the best of it was?<br /> <br /> Both Morgan and Yrtalien stayed on the Autumn Lands. They didn't go to Arcadia at the end of the novels. It meant that they remained and could become my own NPCs. And they sure did! But they never appeared very often in my games, and only in hints. Because I felt that Yrtalien had learned from his defeat, and had been taught some humility, and was now much more intelligent. As for Morgan... well she was already wise beyond her years and a powerful sorceress. So imagine who she could quickly become under the tutelage of the mischievous Liam, the clurichaun.<br /> <br /> Now, it has been announced that Jackie is going to write a new sequel novel from the Immortal Eyes. And that makes me very, very happy, because now, I will revisit all these memories, and I will remember the time when I was a wildler, and when Banality seemed very far away...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","user":"mattboggan","date":". 04-21-2017, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}